    fix(sync): deduplicate audit ledger, store hash not full row (SCHED-GAP-1574)
    
    The DB-SUPA-5 `_audit/*.jsonl` change ledger stored a FULL row image for
    every accepted write, duplicating each memory row next to its data-file
    copy (~287 MB of fleet-wide audit bloat; scheduler namespace `_audit/`
    alone was 784 MB).
    
    The accepted change record now persists a 64-hex SHA-256 `contentHash` of
    the serialized data line (compact JSON + trailing newline, exactly the
    bytes `serializeJsonlLine` appended) INSTEAD of the `row` image; the
    schema becomes {key, contentHash, targetPath, tombstone, schemaVersion,
    ts, ns, table, op, outcome, seq, principal}. The committed data file at
    `targetPath` is the single copy of the row.
    
    Readers updated:
    - `deriveCommitChanges` (realtime replay) resolves the row image from
      `targetPath` at the child commit by content hash — the hash-replay
      form of the target/data-mismatch guard; rewritten, moved, or
      fabricated records fail closed (`CHANGELOG_CORRUPT`) as before.
    - `DerivedChange` carries the resolved `row`, so the v1 SSE wire
      contract (row always present, delete never row: null) is unchanged
      for consumers; live consumers may equally fetch the row from
      DuckBrain by `key`.
    - Legacy row-image audit lines keep validating through the marker
      fields (`isChangeRecordCandidate` accepts contentHash or the legacy
      markers), so pre-existing ledgers replay without migration.
    
    Addresses SCHED-GAP-1574.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
